  "@type": "SemioticProjection",
  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual material describing the violent discussion",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the top_text ('Snuffy and Big Bird discuss the most efficient way to rape the drugged man') as the intended audience for the shocking and harmful message. The meme's structure requires the user to interpret the text as the primary content, and the visual material (Big Bird) serves as a contextual anchor for the absurdity. The projection is onto the textual material because the user must engage with the text to understand the meme's intent, which is to shock through the juxtaposition of innocence (Sesame Street characters) with violence. The phrase 'hush, child' further projects the user into the role of the 'child' being silenced, reinforcing the ironic menace.",
